	How's this for finding a 'back door' (literally!) ?

	Whipped out my trusty ring of levitation from my handy-dandy bag
of holding, and popped it on.  It goes well with my ring of conflict!  Decided
to take a little tour of the waterways, to see what there was to see.  What
should I find when I got across the level but a locked door?  Well, needless
to say, I had my amazing lock-pick out and in use in no time flat!

	There were a couple dragons in there that really were keen on ruining
my good time!  I had to zap 'em with a charm spell, and after that we got along
famously!  

	The only problem is, although I'm intrinsically cold-resistant, the
same does not apply for fire.  Suffice it to say, I do _not_ have a ring for
that, nor could I find one inside the castle (is that by design?).  So when I
decided to drop down one of the many trapdoors I found, well, you *know* what
happened to me!!  And here I thought I'd been SOOOOOOO clever!!  ;)

